PHASE 3 — Architect-Level Observations & Improvements
✅ What's Done Well

Three-layer POM (Page + Module + Test) — clean separation of concerns
Self-healing locators with healing report — resilient selector strategy
Custom reporter with real-time updates and history — production-grade
Multiple reporters — covers all stakeholder needs
Custom fixtures (page objects, modules, authenticatedPage, apiContext) — declarative dependency injection
CI sharding with blob report merging — enterprise-scale parallel execution
Typed test data — JSON + TypeScript interfaces
Lazy locator evaluation — arrow function locators prevent stale references
Hybrid testing patterns — API setup + UI validation

🔧 Gaps to Address (Architect Notes)
1. Only chromium project is active:
firefox, webkit, and mobile-chrome projects are commented out in playwright.config.ts. Re-enable them for cross-browser coverage — CI already installs chromium only, so the workflow would need updating too.
2. No global setup for authentication state:
The framework logs in per-test in beforeEach (or via authenticatedPage fixture). Enterprise frameworks use Playwright's globalSetup to log in ONCE, save storageState, and all tests reuse it:
typescript// playwright.config.ts
globalSetup: './src/fixtures/global.setup.ts',
3. No schema validation on API responses:
typescript// Missing: response schema validation
// Should add: Zod or ajv for runtime response shape validation
const schema = z.object({ title: z.string(), body: z.string() });
const validated = schema.parse(await response.json());
4. Duplicate/stub page & module variants:
LoginPage2/LoginModule2, SignInPage/SignInModule, and HomePage (empty shell) are exploratory. Consolidate to a single pattern per domain — either direct POM or BasePage inheritance — to avoid drift.
5. No database setup/teardown:
No DB seeding or cleanup. For true enterprise testing you'd add a globalSetup that seeds test data and a globalTeardown that cleans it.
6. Rule engine config path:
The rule engine expects rules/framework-rule-engine.json. Keep this file in sync with the rules/ folder (the file currently lives in "rules copy/" — move it to rules/ so scripts/rule-engine.js finds it).

